        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/258725120?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h2 dir=\"auto\">Description</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This updates the Web Storage API documentation to mention <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Privacy/Guides/State_Partitioning\" rel=\"nofollow\">state partitioning</a>, which modern browsers use to partition storage by top-level site when accessed from third-party contexts.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Files changed</h3>\n<ol dir=\"auto\">\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>localStorage</strong> (): Added a paragraph in the Description section explaining that localStorage is subject to state partitioning when accessed from third-party contexts.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>sessionStorage</strong> (): Corrected the opening paragraph which previously stated that localStorage is partitioned by origin only. Added a note about state partitioning affecting both localStorage and sessionStorage.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Web Storage API overview</strong> (): Corrected the bullet point that claimed localStorage is partitioned by origin only. Added information about state partitioning.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p dir=\"auto\">These changes address the issue that the documentation incorrectly states localStorage is partitioned by origin only, which is no longer accurate due to state partitioning mechanisms in modern browsers.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #43255.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3994738752\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43255\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43255/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43255\">#43255</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45209",
            "title": "Add state partitioning notes to Web Storage API documentation",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-18T03:13:58.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-18T03:13:31.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "morning-verlu",
                "url": "https://github.com/morning-verlu"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/258725120?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h2 dir=\"auto\">Description</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds an Accessibility section to the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/ElementInternals/labels\" rel=\"nofollow\">ElementInternals.labels</a> page, documenting that screen reader support for labels associated via  varies by browser.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Key points covered:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>In most browsers, the label is announced when the custom element receives focus</li>\n<li>Safari does not reliably narrate labels associated via  for form-associated custom elements (referencing <a href=\"https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=259124\" rel=\"nofollow\">WebKit bug 259124</a>)</li>\n<li>Developers should consider supplementing with ARIA attributes (, ) for robust cross-browser support</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #44395.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4621852846\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44395\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/44395/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44395\">#44395</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45208",
            "title": "Add accessibility note for screen reader support to ElementInternals.labels",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-18T03:03:13.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-18T03:02:51.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "morning-verlu",
                "url": "https://github.com/morning-verlu"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF155 supports the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/GPUSupportedFeatures#available_features\" rel=\"nofollow\">dual-source blending</a> feature in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1924328\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1924328</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds the feature for Firefox desktop (FF android doesn't support the parent feature).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Note that I have explained what it allows you to specifically use, rather than what it allows you to do - because that's what the existing docs do, and because I don't know enough about Web GPU to be sure of what AIs tell me.<br>\nAccording to Gemini this allows you to blend two sources into a destination texture: your source and a per-channel mask. This allows control over the mixing of your source into particular colour channels rather than equally to all channels. Apprarently can be useful for some fonts etc.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5170075051\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45176\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45176/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45176\">#45176</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45207",
            "title": "FF155 Relnote: WebGPU dual-source-blending",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-18T01:31:33.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-18T01:30:02.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF155 supports web rtc error events with the <code class=\"notranslate\">sctp-error</code> type fired at a data channel with <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/RTCError/errorDetail\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">RTCError.errorDetail</code></a> set to <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/RTCError/errorDetail#sctp-failure\" rel=\"nofollow\">\"sctp-failure\"</a> in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1814460\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1814460</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds the release note. Note that <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/RTCErrorEvent\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">RTCErrorEvent</code></a> and its <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/RTCError\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">RTCError</code></a> property are also supported on dedicated workers so this is mentioned (it is non-standard nowm, but coming to the spec).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5170074351\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45175\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45175/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45175\">#45175</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45206",
            "title": "FF155 Relnote: RTCError \"sctp-failure\" detail",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-18T00:44:14.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-18T00:42:32.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF155 adds support for <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/RTCErrorEvent\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">RTCErrorEvent</code></a> to be fired in dedicated workers (but not other workers) and hence it is exposed on them, along with the property <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/RTCError\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">RTCError</code></a>. See <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1814460\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1814460</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds the macro to methods.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Note that this is not in the spec yet, but is approved <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3997825755\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/w3c/webrtc-pc/issues/3092\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/w3c/webrtc-pc/issues/3092/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/w3c/webrtc-pc/issues/3092\">w3c/webrtc-pc#3092</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5170074351\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45175\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45175/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45175\">#45175</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45205",
            "title": "FF155 RTCError{Event} also supported on workers",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-17T23:41:34.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-17T23:39:55.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69888?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Who knew a little property could be so complicated?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR includes the creation of one new reference page:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">column-rule-inset-cap-end</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Spec: <a href=\"https://drafts.csswg.org/css-gaps-1/#propdef-column-rule-inset-cap-end\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://drafts.csswg.org/css-gaps-1/#propdef-column-rule-inset-cap-end</a><br>\nThe <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Gaps\" rel=\"nofollow\">CSS gaps module page</a> is already live.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Part of <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4718339915\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/openwebdocs/project/issues/238\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/openwebdocs/project/issues/238/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/openwebdocs/project/issues/238\">openwebdocs/project#238</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45204",
            "title": "New page: column-rule-inset-cap-end",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-17T22:07:51.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-17T21:32:42.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "estelle",
                "url": "https://github.com/estelle"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Part of <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5170081223\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45186\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45186/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45186\">#45186</a></p>",
